  "manual": "Spellcaster spell-counter control built on the Endymion engine. You bank Spell Counters every time you cast, then cash them in for a 2700 boss and repeatable removal.\n\n## The engine (do this first)\n- **Magical Citadel of Endymion** (Field Spell) is the heart: every Spell you *resolve* banks 1 Spell Counter on it, it soaks counters off any counter-card that dies, and it can pay counter-costs for your other cards. Open on it (fetch with **Terraforming**) and just start casting.\n- **Win line:** once Citadel holds 6 counters, Special Summon **Endymion, the Master Magician** (2700) by removing all 6 — on summon add a Spell back from GY, and every turn after, discard 1 Spell to **destroy ANY 1 card** on the field. That recurring pop is your control loop; feed it with Spells you've already used.\n- **Counter accelerants (stack these):** **Spell Power Grasp** places a counter AND fetches the next copy (chains its own draw of gas); **Apprentice Magician** drops a counter on summon; **Breaker** / **Defender** each place 1 on Normal Summon; **Pitch-Black Power Stone** banks 3 and ferries them one-per-turn onto Citadel. **Magical Exemplar** banks 2 per Spell and dumps them to revive a Spellcaster from hand/GY (re-summon a popped Endymion or Breaker).\n\n## Payoffs that spend counters\n- **Breaker the Magical Warrior** — summon, then pop a Spell/Trap for free (1600, briefly 1900).\n- **Blast Magician** — remove counters to snipe a monster (counters x700 ATK cap).\n- **Dark Red Enchanter** — enters with 2 counters, +300 ATK each, and rips a random card from their hand.\n- **Mythical Beast Cerberus** — grows +500 per counter (swings huge, but dumps its own counters after battle).\n\n## Spellcaster tricks\n- **Magical Dimension** is the glue: control any Spellcaster, tribute a monster, Special Summon a Spellcaster from hand AND destroy a monster — tribute a spent **Apprentice Magician** / **Old Vindictive Magician** to drop **Endymion** and blow something up at instant speed.\n- **Defender, the Magical Knight** shields your Spellcasters from destruction (pay 1 counter each). **Old Vindictive Magician** flips to pop a monster. **Summoner Monk** discards a Spell to swarm a Level 4. **Magician's Circle** searches a Spellcaster on any attack. **Magicians Unite** pumps one Spellcaster to 3000 for a finisher.\n- **Field Barrier** locks Citadel down — it can't be destroyed and the opponent can't set their own Field Spell.\n\n## Control shell\n- Board wipes / removal: **Fissure**, **Swords of Revealing Light**, **Magic Cylinder**, **Enemy Controller**, **Book of Moon**.\n- Tempo & reuse: **Giant Trunade** (bounce your own backrow to re-cast for more counters), **Twister**.\n- Equips for a beater: **Mage Power**, **Malevolent Nuzzler**, **Mist Body** (untargetable-by-destruction wall).\n- **Royal Magical Library** turns your Spell spam into draws (3 counters -> draw). **Magical Blast** burns 200 per Spellcaster and recurs itself.\n\n## Weaknesses\n- ⚠ Slow: you need to survive long enough to bank 6 counters — fast aggro can race you before Endymion lands.\n- ⚠ Field-Spell dependent: if Citadel is destroyed before **Field Barrier** protects it (Mystical Space Typhoon, an opposing Field Spell, etc.), the engine sputters.\n- ⚠ **Tower of Babel** is anti-synergy with your own gameplan — its 4th Spell Counter blasts *the player who cast that Spell*, i.e. YOU, the spell-spammer. Many pilots cut it; play around it or leave it in the box.\n- ⚠ Endymion is one fat target — Bottomless / banish / bounce removes your payoff and the counters spent to summon it.",
